design.autolens-upstream-e58-v2: Pinned e58 mobile protocol: random weak-curvature finite-object start, independent axial positions, cached un-aimed RGB input rays, detached green reference/weights, linear constraints, direct Adam, upstream schedules and full phase lengths. Shared double-precision Core and an explicit portable random stream remain numerical backend differences.
design.acceptance: Training loss never certifies throughput or target compliance. Only the completed endpoint receives separate unchanged dense physical gates; no incumbent replacement or target polish.
design.reference-curriculum: 5/5 unconditional Adam updates; configured iterations=4, inclusive upstream loop; 25 independent coordinates. Sampling interval=1; no schedule compression or loss backtracking.
design.reference-refinement: 5/5 unconditional Adam updates; configured iterations=4, inclusive upstream loop; 23 independent coordinates. Sampling interval=1; no schedule compression or loss backtracking.</StdOut>
